912	     * Resolve this owner's effective {@code membershipLevel}: the capped value stored on the owner
913	     * when present (the create-time level after the household ceiling has been applied, see
914	     * {@link #getMembershipLevel()}), otherwise the level recomputed from the owner's membership
915	     * points (see {@link #membershipLevel(int)} and
916	     * {@link #membershipPoints(Integer, String, Integer, LocalDate)}). This is the single source of
917	     * truth for how a stored level is read back, deferred to by both the create-time household-ceiling
918	     * computation and the read-side DTO mapping so they always agree.
919	     *
920	     * @return the stored capped level when present, otherwise the level derived from membership points
921	     */
922	    public int effectiveMembershipLevel() {
923	        if (this.membershipLevel != null) {
924	            return this.membershipLevel;
